# AgentDraven.instructions (SPRK student mentor)

This is the student-facing companion to enterprise `AgentDraven.instructions` in the private MERIT vault. It keeps the mentor voice and learning habits without copying private operator content.

## Who this is for

Students, classroom facilitators, and coding agents helping in `SPRK-Hello-Repo`.

## Read order

1. [README.md](README.md) — pick a mission and create your branch first.
2. [docs/README.md](docs/README.md) — documentation hub.
3. [MERIT.instructions](MERIT.instructions) — mission folder naming and repo rules.
4. [docs/SPRK_Student_AgenticOps_Guide.md](docs/SPRK_Student_AgenticOps_Guide.md) — how enterprise MERIT maps to this classroom repo.
5. [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) — validation commands and agent closeout.
6. The mission you are building: `missions/<NN-GameName-mode>/docs/MISSION_GUIDE.md`.

## Mentor habits

- Play the mission before editing it.
- Make one small visible change, then run it again.
- Keep work on your own branch, not `main`.
- Use the three tabs (`RealTime`, `X-Ray Vision`, `Baseline Status`) to understand what changed.
- Prefer clear student language over jargon.

## Mission naming reminder

Always use `NN-GameName-<mode-label>` under `missions/`. Example: `10-SpaceInvaders-1P-nP`, not `10-Space-Invaders`.

## Branch and PR discipline

Use one branch and one PR per task. Review changes, conflict fixes, validation refreshes, and follow-up edits stay on that same PR. If duplicate PRs appear for the same task, choose the canonical PR, move useful changes there, and close the duplicates.

When reporting work, name the canonical branch and PR so students and agents know where forward progress lives.

## Git and GitHub help

- Guided helper: [docs/SPRK_Guided_Workflow_Helper.md](docs/SPRK_Guided_Workflow_Helper.md) and `npm run workflow`
- Branch rules: [docs/SPRK_Git_Repository_UserGuide.md](docs/SPRK_Git_Repository_UserGuide.md)

## When something fails

1. Read the message — look for `[FAIL]` and the suggested next step.
2. Confirm the mission folder name matches [MERIT.instructions](MERIT.instructions).
3. Stop any old `python server.py` on the same port.
4. From repo root: `npm run setup:missions` then `npm run validate` (or the single-mission `npm run test:<mission>` script).

## Handoff format (Done / State / Next)

Use three short sections when you finish a slice of work:

```markdown
Done
- What changed

State
- What passed or failed (include test command)

Next
- What someone should try in the browser or classroom
```

See [ops/README.md](ops/README.md) for hygiene checks before commit.

## Where enterprise instructions live

Full enterprise `MERIT.instructions` and `AgentDraven.instructions` remain in the private MERIT Obsidian vault. This repository intentionally carries only the student-safe subset above so learners can study AgenticOps without private secrets or operator-only paths.

For every guide in this repo, use [docs/README.md](docs/README.md). When linking to a **section**, follow [MERIT.instructions — Documentation links](MERIT.instructions#documentation-links-required) [[MERIT.instructions#Documentation links (required)]] (obsidian): portable Markdown link plus `[[Note#Heading]] (obsidian)`.
